<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anne Hutchinson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1591–1643</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anne Hutchinson was an English-born Puritan spiritual adviser in the Massachusetts Bay Colony. Her religious meetings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> and her teaching on grace led to the Antinomian Controversy, and in 1638 she was tried and banished. With her followers she founded Portsmouth in what became Rhode Island; she was later killed in an attack by Native Americans in New Netherland in 1643.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-hutchinson.jpg" alt="Anne Hutchinson" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edwin Austin Abbey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anne_Hutchinson_on_Trial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
